{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he passed</b> — [a form of] רוח." "<b>The sea</b> — the sense is that the sea and the river of Egypt dry up, so as to make a way for the redeemed to cross from Assyria, for by sea they come to the river, to Egypt, and from there to the land of Israel. Thus Isaiah said: \"And HaShem will utterly destroy the tongue of the sea of Egypt, and wave His hand over the river\" — this is the river of Egypt — and there it is written: \"And there shall be a highway for the remnant of His people that remains from Assyria.\"" "<b>And the pride of Assyria brought down</b> — that they not rule over Israel, for He casts the terror of the Chasdim upon them, and likewise Egypt."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:41.611775094Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}